WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.830
- Let's close out with something

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:04.710
we grabbed off social media
perfect for the holidays.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.045
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:06.045 --> 00:00:08.640
(upbeat music)
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.590
Usually when you picture Santa

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.900
he's in his reindeer powdered sleigh,

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.410
lugging bundles of toys and
battling the winter weather.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.800
You don't envision hundreds
of surfers dressed up as Santa

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.480
and his elves riding the waves

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.640
on Florida's East Coast. (chuckles)

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.350
But that happens every year

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:28.740
with thousands of onlookers
crowding the beach to watch.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.860
We have the founder of this
giant event on the line.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:34.114
Hi, George. This is so super cool.

00:00:34.114 --> 00:00:35.010
(audience applauds)

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.510
So it started-
- Hey, Kelly.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.970
- Small with your son, right?

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.450
- Yeah. I was born here
in the Cocoa Beach area

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.000
here on Florida's Space Coast.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.390
And Cocoa Beach is known as the small wave

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.744
surfing capital of the world.

00:00:50.744 --> 00:00:51.577
- Oh, wow.

00:00:51.577 --> 00:00:54.210
- I'm close to 60 years old.
(audience applauding)

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:56.980
Back in 2009, my wife made me this

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.540
awesome surfing Santa outfit.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.640
The newspaper took a picture

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:07.640
and published it and labeled
the picture Surfing Santa.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:13.340
Over the years, the event has
grown and grown and grown.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.283
It's unbelievable.

00:01:14.283 --> 00:01:16.140
(audience applauding)
- Oh, that's so cool.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:19.710
I love that, how that started
out and then it became this,

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.270
you created something so cool

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.950
and magical for so many people.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.260
So, it's not just for fun though, right?

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.090
You're doing good as well, right?

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:30.810
- Yeah. On Christmas Eve,
we will have at least

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:35.810
400 people join us on
December 24th dressed to surf.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.040
And our crowd, it'll exceed 10,000 people.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.900
We have a costume contest.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.730
There's live music.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:47.850
We have Hawaiian dancers
that entertain us.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:50.922
And everybody is smiling.

00:01:50.922 --> 00:01:52.907
It's-
- That is so cool, man.

00:01:52.907 --> 00:01:54.147
- Really, really fun.

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:55.530
(audience applauding)

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.470
- Your family created this
long-lasting tradition

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:00.630
that's probably gonna carry on, like,

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:01.980
for the next generation,
the next generation.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:03.660
It's such a cool thing, George.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:06.360
Thank you so much for starting
this and sharing this.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.366
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:08.366 --> 00:02:09.199
(audience applauding)
(bell dings)

00:02:09.199 --> 00:02:10.032
- Oh, thank you.

00:02:10.032 --> 00:02:10.865
- Oh, absolutely.

00:02:10.865 --> 00:02:11.698
And that's not all.

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:14.010
Our season-long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of FriXion,

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:16.200
the go-to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.786
want to celebrate those creating
fearlessly just like you.

00:02:19.786 --> 00:02:21.360
So they're gonna be writing you a check

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.210
for a thousand dollars to
the Florida Surf Museum.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.320
How's that sound?
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:28.140
- Oh yeah! Thank you. That's great.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.810
- Oh man, thank you so much
for joining us, George.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:31.643
Have a good one.

00:02:31.643 --> 00:02:33.570
And thank you to all our guests today.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:36.780
Jewel, Andrea Savage, Jaylen, Julian,

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:39.090
Ron Peters, and Lawrence Zarian.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:41.160
From my home to yours, have a great day,

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.263
and if it's not, well, try and change it.

